<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frances Nelson, Viscountess Nelson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1831</span> · Also known as Fanny Nelson, Frances Nisbet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">Frances</a> Nelson, Viscountess Nelson, born Frances Woolward on Nevis, was the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a>. Widowed after her first marriage to the physician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah">Josiah</a> Nisbet, she married Nelson on Nevis in March 1787. The couple separated in 1801 after Nelson's affair with Emma Hamilton became public, and she lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> until her death in 1831.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frances-nelson-viscountess-nelson.jpg" alt="Frances Nelson, Viscountess Nelson" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lady_Nelson_-_Project_Gutenberg_eText_16914.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
